        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0293" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.54/298.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 392.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In acknowledging the receipt of the
                    Department’s instruction No. 175 of September 29, 1911, relating to a proposed
                    arrangement with the French Government for the reciprocal protection of literary
                    and artistic property in China, I have the honor to send enclosed copies of the
                    notes recently exchanged with the French Legation following the precedents
                    established for the protection of trademarks among foreigners in China.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to state further that if these notes meet with your approval I
                    shall approach the other legations in Peking in compliance with your instruction
                    acknowledged above, with a view to concluding similar agreements with their
                    respective governments.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d300-a1.xml" xpointer="d300-a1"/>
